// =============================================================================
// simulation.mx3.in -- single-pulse free-decay template. Rendered and executed once
// per pulse: process working directory = runs/<pulse_id>/, rendered script fixed name
// simulation.mx3; MuMax3 default native output directory simulation.out/
// (contract-required: table.txt, m_t0.ovf, m_tfinal.ovf); run.log and trajectory.csv
// are written by the pipeline at the pulse directory root. Rendered from the same
// config as equilibrium.mx3.in (shared model section byte-identical).
// Command syntax follows the MuMax3 3.12 official API documentation; the execution
// chain (sampling timing, field switch-off instant, and LoadFile behavior) has been
// minimally validated by a short test-only pilot (8x4x1, 1 pulse, 3 samples). The
// numerical protocol (EdgeSmooth/solver/MaxErr/MaxDt/GammaLL) is explicitly injected
// from the YAML numerics block via the shared model section; diagnostics (DIAGNOSTIC
// stdout lines) go to run.log; convergence/QC validation remains to be done, and
// until then this must not be used for formal research data.
// =============================================================================

// 1. Shared model section: identical to section 1 of equilibrium.mx3.in (the single
//    renderer _render_model_setup keeps the numerical protocol/grid/ellipsoid
//    geometry/material from drifting; alpha is not part of the shared section).
{{MODEL_SETUP}}

// 2. Load the shared equilibrium state (fixed relative path, relative to
//    runs/<pulse_id>/); load only, never relax again: the equilibrium state is
//    frozen in the OVF.
m.LoadFile("../../equilibrium/equilibrium.out/equilibrium.ovf")

// 3. Experimental true alpha (inversion target; the equilibrium state is frozen in
//    the OVF, so no auxiliary damping may be used here)
alpha = {{ALPHA}}

// 4. Rectangular pulse and exact field switch-off. First disable automatic table
//    saving (sampling rows are produced only by manual TableSave calls), then apply,
//    from t=0, a constant external field (the three runtime SI components in T are
//    computed by the renderer from amplitude and direction) held for pulse_duration s
//    and then set exactly to 0.
TableAutoSave(0)
B_ext = vector({{B_EXT_X_T}}, {{B_EXT_Y_T}}, {{B_EXT_Z_T}})
Run({{PULSE_DURATION_S}})
B_ext = vector(0, 0, 0)

// 5. Sampling static contract (minimally executed and validated by the short
//    test-only pilot; numerical-protocol convergence/QC validation remains to be
//    done): immediately after switch-off, a TableSave call (sample_index=0, t_s=0)
//    and save m_t0.ovf (QC) -> then run sample_count-1 times
//    Run(sample_interval)+TableSave -> save m_tfinal.ovf at the last point (QC);
//    table.txt rows correspond to integer indices in sampling order.
TableSave()
SaveAs(m, "m_t0")
for i := 1; i < {{SAMPLE_COUNT}}; i++ {
	Run({{SAMPLE_INTERVAL_S}})
	TableSave()
}
SaveAs(m, "m_tfinal")

// 6. Diagnostics go to run.log via stdout (DIAGNOSTIC prefix for easy lookup);
//    PeakErr is this process's historical peak error, LastErr the last-step error,
//    dt is in s, and step/NEval are counts.
print("DIAGNOSTIC PeakErr=", PeakErr, " LastErr=", LastErr, " dt_s=", dt, " step=", step, " NEval=", NEval)
